{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1791181929,"nonce":"AzpErPd4iRI+audvx51WBW/umeo=","target":"ed801104a1f2997016acf2f59bd2e09041429ea21c71941fff75be34226677e4","message":"A layer's `expand` was a layer, or the string `\"self\"` to repeat the layer as far down as the relation goes. Every other string in that slot names a relation, so `\"self\"` read as a relation that does not exist, and \"the layer below inherits the one above\" is an odd frame across types that do not share fields. It is now a number: `\"expand\": N` is this same layer again N more levels down, `\"expand\": 0` every level down. A number at the top level, a negative or a fraction are refused. `view/expand.go`, `tui/nest.go`, `doc/design/terminal-renderer.md` Nesting.","files":null}]}